# Routes review by path. Copy to .github/CODEOWNERS (or your host's equivalent).
#
# READ THIS FIRST: **CODEOWNERS ALONE DOES NOTHING.** Your host uses it to REQUEST reviews, not to
# require them. It becomes a control only when branch protection turns on "require review from code
# owners". Until then every line here is a polite suggestion anyone can merge past — which is worth
# knowing, because a code-owners file reads like a control and is not one.
#
# IF YOU ARE A SINGLE MAINTAINER, write yourself and say so in a comment. Inventing team handles that
# do not exist produces silently broken review requests, which is worse than one honest name.

*                       @your-handle

# ── Paths where a mistake is expensive. Same owner today; the SPLIT is the point, so they are already
#    carved out for whenever there is someone else to assign them to. ──

# The enforcement machinery. A change that weakens a gate is the one least likely to announce itself
# in a diff — it looks like a small config edit.
/tools/gates/           @your-handle
/tools/qa/              @your-handle
/.githooks/             @your-handle

# CI, secret scanning, and this file — anything that can turn a control off.
/.github/               @your-handle
/.gitleaks.toml         @your-handle

# Dependency pinning and build reproducibility.
/*.lock                 @your-handle
